I think I could mentor a bit, but someone else should be the admin.

I could provide a bunch of tasks:

1. Code: one medium (refactoring), possibly a bunch of hard ones.
2. Documentation: one medium but possibly tedious (move documentation
to roxygen2)
3. Outreach:  2 project web pages on r-forge to polish (easy)
4. Quality Assurance: two medium
5. Research: produce a graph/tree of R packages providing GUI
6. Training:  correction/readability checking of manuals
7. Translation:
8. User interface:

Claudia

